      "comment" : "Accessibility screen section header: the ways to take a photo besides the on-screen shutter.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Taking the Photo" : {
      "comment" : "Timing in the photo details: from pressing the shutter to the camera returning the photo.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Telephoto" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a rear telephoto camera lens.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The battery is low." : {
      "comment" : "Announced to VoiceOver when the battery is low and the device isn't charging.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera couldn't start. Try another lens." : {
      "comment" : "Shown over the viewfinder when the camera fails to start.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera is in use by another app or a call. It comes back when that ends." : {
      "comment" : "Shown over the viewfinder when another app or a phone or video call is using the camera.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera is paused by the system. It comes back by itself." : {
      "comment" : "Shown over the viewfinder when the system pauses the camera for another reason.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera is paused to let your device cool down." : {
      "comment" : "Shown over the viewfinder when the device is too hot to run the camera.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera is taking photos. Try again when it's done." : {
      "comment" : "Shown when a settings preset can't be applied, and VoiceOver hint of a dimmed lens button, during a countdown, burst, series or astro run.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera isn't on, so the lens and camera values didn't change." : {
      "comment" : "Shown after applying a settings preset before the camera is allowed or started.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera isn't sending a picture." : {
      "comment" : "Shown over the viewfinder when the camera runs but every picture it delivers is blank, even after the app restarted the camera.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera opens with only the viewfinder and the shutter. Warnings about the photo always show." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the clean view switch.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera works only when nope. fills the screen." : {
      "comment" : "Shown on iPad in Split View, Slide Over or Stage Manager. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The camera's live values, such as shutter, ISO, focus and white balance." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Live Camera Readout switch. ISO is the usual camera abbreviation.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The frames take longer than their exposure time: each one also needs time to save. They stop early if storage runs out, the battery is nearly empty, or the camera stops." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the estimates in the night sky helper's settings.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The light is off: the system didn't allow it, for example because the device is too warm. Turn Light off and on again in Q to try again, or choose a lower brightness." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Light Unavailable warning. Light is the name of a camera control; Q is the letter on the Quick Menu button beside the shutter: keep \"Q\" unchanged. Replaces the sentence that named Quick Controls.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The next photo won't fit. Free up storage on this device to keep taking photos." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation of the Storage Full warning on the camera: saving another photo would fail until the person frees storage.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The photo wasn't taken. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Shown when taking a photo failed.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The subject may be too close to focus. Try %@." : {
      "comment" : "Hint on the camera when autofocus can't get close enough. The value is a lens name such as Ultra Wide.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The volume buttons, and the Camera Control on iPhones that have one, take a photo." : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility screen: hardware buttons work as the shutter. Camera Control is Apple's name for the camera button on recent iPhones.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "These lenses have no RAW, so each photo is the phone's processed file. A larger size has more pixels and bigger files. The smallest size is the default." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Photo Size screen. RAW is a file format name. On iPad the English names the iPad, and on other devices it says \"device\"; translate each variant. Draft for the Honesty review.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "device" : {
              "ipad" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "These lenses have no RAW, so each photo is the iPad's processed file. A larger size has more pixels and bigger files. The smallest size is the default."
                }
              },
              "iphone" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "These lenses have no RAW, so each photo is the phone's processed file. A larger size has more pixels and bigger files. The smallest size is the default."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "These lenses have no RAW, so each photo is the device's processed file. A larger size has more pixels and bigger files. The smallest size is the default."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Third-Party Notices" : {
      "comment" : "Section header for notices required by other licenses.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Thirds" : {
      "comment" : "Grid style: two lines each way, at thirds (rule of thirds).",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "This device has no camera that nope. can use." : {
      "comment" : "Explains that the device has no usable camera. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "This device has no lens like the preset's, so the lens didn't change." : {
      "comment" : "Shown after applying a settings preset saved with a lens this device doesn't have.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "This lens has a fixed aperture." : {
      "comment" : "Explains why the aperture can't be changed on this lens.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "This lens: %@" : {
      "comment" : "The range of a control on the selected lens, for example This lens: 54 – 12,096.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "This preset can't be read." : {
      "comment" : "Shown when a saved settings preset is damaged and can't be applied.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tilted %@ clockwise" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver value of the horizon level: how far the device is turned clockwise from level. The value is an angle such as 3°.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tilted %@ counterclockwise" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver value of the horizon level: how far the device is turned counterclockwise from level. The value is an angle such as 3°.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Timer, above the shutter, sets a self-timer of 3 or 10 seconds. Burst is beside it. VoiceOver says each second of the countdown." : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility page, Self-Timer and Burst: where the self-timer and burst are on the camera. Timer and Burst are words on the drive strip above the shutter; use their translations. VoiceOver is Apple's screen reader; keep the name unchanged. Replaces the sentence that named Quick Controls.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Timing" : {
      "comment" : "Heading in the photo details: how long each step of taking and saving the photo took, in milliseconds.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tint" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the white balance tint slider (green to magenta).",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "To take photos, turn on camera access for nope. in the Settings app." : {
      "comment" : "Explains how to allow camera access after it was declined. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged: it is the app's name.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Torch" : {
      "comment" : "Live readout line: the torch (steady light) level, as a percentage, or Off.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Try Again" : {
      "comment" : "Button on the message about a photo that wasn't taken or saved: takes the photo again.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Tungsten" : {
      "comment" : "White balance preset for incandescent (tungsten) light.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Turn off Astro to start interval shooting." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under the disabled Start button of interval shooting while the night sky helper is on. Astro is the helper's name on the camera.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Turn Off Close-Up" : {
      "comment" : "Action of the Close-Up pill on the camera: lets autofocus focus at any distance again.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Turn Off Compare" : {
      "comment" : "Action of the Compare pill on the camera: turns the comparison shot off.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Turn Off Far Focus" : {
      "comment" : "Action of the Far Focus pill on the camera: lets autofocus focus at any distance again.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Turn Off Flash" : {
      "comment" : "Action of the flash pill on the camera: the flash no longer fires.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Turn Off Light" : {
      "comment" : "Action of the Light pill on the camera: turns the light (torch) off.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Turn Off Magnifier" : {
      "comment" : "Action of the magnifier pill on the camera: shows the whole viewfinder again.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ultra Wide" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the rear ultra wide camera lens.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Undo" : {
      "comment" : "Button that returns every setting to what it was before the preset was applied.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Unlock" : {
      "comment" : "Action of the lock pill on the camera: unlocks exposure and focus.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Unlock Focus and Exposure" : {
      "comment" : "Button and VoiceOver action on the camera: returns focus and exposure to automatic.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Use %lld characters or fewer." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under the preset name field when the name is too long. The placeholder is the most characters allowed.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Use a tripod. Turn on Magnify to check focus on a bright star or a distant light, and fine-tune it with the Focus control." : {
      "comment" : "Tip in the night sky helper's settings. Magnify and Focus are the names of the camera's focus magnifier and manual focus control.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Use Standard Shutter" : {
      "comment" : "Action of the fast shutter pill on the camera: returns the fast shutter choice to Standard.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Version" : {
      "comment" : "Label for the app's version number.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Viewfinder" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver name of the live camera view.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Viewfinder Overlays" : {
      "comment" : "Settings row and screen title: the grid, level, focus peaking, histogram and live readout drawn over the viewfinder.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "VoiceOver says when each photo is saved and signed, or what went wrong." : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility screen: spoken feedback. VoiceOver is Apple's screen reader; keep the name unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "WB" : {
      "comment" : "Short label of the white balance control in the control grid.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "What's in This Photo" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the sheet that lists the facts read back from the photo nope. just saved: files, exposure, signature, details kept and removed.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "When Astro turns Night Mode on, it stays on after you leave Astro instead of turning off again." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the Keep Night Mode After Astro switch. Astro is the night sky drive mode; Night Mode is the name of nope.'s switch. Use their translations.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "White Balance" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the white balance (color temperature) control.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "White Balance / Tint" : {
      "comment" : "Live readout line: the white balance temperature in kelvin and the tint, then how white balance is controlled now (Auto or Locked).",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Whole Frame" : {
      "comment" : "Metering mode: the camera measures the whole frame.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Wide" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the rear wide (main) camera lens.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "With a hardware keyboard, the Space bar takes a photo." : {
      "comment" : "Accessibility screen: a connected keyboard's Space bar works as the shutter.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Zero shutter lag" : {
      "comment" : "Live readout: the camera feature that takes the photo from frames buffered before the press.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Zoom In" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the compare view: enlarges both photos together, to see detail, noise and sharpening.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Zoom Out" : {
      "comment" : "Button in the compare view: shows more of both photos.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Stop After" : {
      "comment" : "Picker for what ends an interval series: a number of photos, or a time.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Number of Photos" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the Stop After picker of interval shooting: the series stops once it has taken the chosen number of photos.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Time" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the Stop After picker of interval shooting: the series stops once the chosen hours and minutes have passed.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Hours" : {
      "comment" : "Picker for the whole hours of the time an interval series runs before it stops.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Minutes" : {
      "comment" : "Picker for the minutes, past the whole hours, of the time an interval series runs before it stops.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "At most %lld" : {
      "comment" : "The most photos an interval series that stops after a time can take: one at the start and one after each interval that starts before the time is up. Saving each photo adds time, so it usually takes fewer. The number is a count of photos, at least 2.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "The time keeps running while the series is paused, so the series ends on time." : {
      "comment" : "Explains interval shooting that stops after a time: if nope. leaves the screen or the camera is interrupted, the time still counts, and the series ends at the time it would have ended. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged if used.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Choose an interval shorter than the time." : {
      "comment" : "Shown on the interval card and under the disabled Start button when the series stops after a time that is no longer than the time between photos, so it would take only one photo.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Every %@, for %@" : {
      "comment" : "Interval card on the camera, before a series that stops after a time starts: the time between photos, then how long the series runs. Both placeholders are durations formatted by the system, such as \"10 seconds\" and \"1 hour, 30 minutes\".",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "Ends at %@" : {
      "comment" : "Interval card on the camera while a series that stops after a time is paused: the time on the clock when it ends, such as 9:41 PM, with the day of the week when it is not today. Formatted by the system.",
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "%lld photos taken · %@ left" : {
      "comment" : "Interval shooting progress for a series that stops after a time: how many photos are taken so far, and the time left. The number is a count of photos; the placeholder is the time left, such as \"1 hr, 12 min\", formatted by the system.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "%#@photos@ · %2$@ left"
          },
          "substitutions" : {
            "photos" : {
              "argNum" : 1,
              "formatSpecifier" : "lld",
              "variations" : {
                "plural" : {
                  "one" : {
                    "stringUnit" : {
                      "state" : "translated",
                      "value" : "%arg photo taken"
                    }
                  },
                  "other" : {
                    "stringUnit" : {
                      "state" : "translated",
                      "value" : "%arg photos taken"
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Paused: %lld photos taken · %@ left" : {
      "comment" : "Interval shooting that stops after a time, paused because the camera is paused (for example by a call) or nope. is in the background: it continues when the camera is back, and its time keeps running meanwhile. The number is a count of photos; the placeholder is the time left, such as \"1 hr, 12 min\", formatted by the system. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Paused: %#@photos@ · %2$@ left"
          },
          "substitutions" : {
